      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by $33$, we need to determine the smallest four-digit number and the largest number less than it that is divisible by $33$. \n\nThe smallest four-digit number is $1000$. To find the largest number less than $1000$ that is divisible by $33$, we divide $1000$ by $33$ and round down to the nearest whole number. \n\n$$\\frac{1000}{33} \\approx 30 \\hspace{1mm}\\text{with a remainder of} \\hspace{1mm} 10$$\n\nThen we can multiply $33$ by $30$ and add the remainder:\n\n$$33\\cdot 30 + 10 = 990+10 = 1000$$\n\nSince $1000$ is the largest four-digit number that is divisible by $33$, we need to subtract $3$ from it. The largest four-digit number divisible by $33$ is:\n\n$$1000 - 3 \\boxed{997}$$",
